 "data": {
  "why": "A portable air conditioner cut open in a living room in front of the window: a fan blows over a cold coil, the coil sweats onto the floor, a tray and hose fix it, the coil warms, a compressor keeps it cold, and the heat goes out of the window through a duct. The camera opens close on the fan and coil, stays mid on the machine, and ends on the room with the unit running calmly.",
  "story": {
   "title": "How an air conditioner works",
   "hero": "an air conditioner",
   "parts": [
    "fan",
    "cold coil",
    "drip tray",
    "drain hose",
    "compressor",
    "pipes",
    "hot coil",
    "window duct",
